  "v638_deficit": "How to read the figure. Black points show observed counts divided by the bin width, with sqrt(N) count-only errors. The blue curve is the GP sideband prediction, and its band is one marginal standard deviation of the background constraint; it is not a post-fit confidence band. Gold is the profiled background-only fit. Green is the background component of the signed signal-plus-background fit, and red is its total. In the lower panel the same GP mean is subtracted from data and backgrounds; purple isolates the signed signal contribution. All profiled curves are restricted to the likelihood bins, which are excluded from GP training. The quoted yield is full-selected and signed, with a conditional Hessian error. The fitted signal is negative: it describes a deficit, and the excess statistic is q0=0. The background-only toy probability uses the lower tail of the signed likelihood root. The region was selected using the same observed scan; neither the asymptotic nor toy probability includes the mass-search selection. Toy rank probabilities use the add-one rule, while the stated exact two-sided 95% Clopper\u2013Pearson interval describes the underlying exceedance fraction. Disjoint fitted intervals still share GP sidebands and are not independent measurements."
